nvironment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:bed6e6de92146f4dbe54cbaa419f632292cca06b0f487f298dbfd5abfd0d6ddf","file":"preprints/Nonuniqueness-for-the-periodic-hard-sphere-Boltzmann-equation-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":55,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"df43532cfd684943f8ba13d7229f8406ae85d8cad3d29dd1a6bf959449ebff9a","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Nonuniqueness-for-the-periodic-hard-sphere-Boltzmann-equation-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:bed6e6de92146f4dbe54cbaa419f632292cca06b0f487f298dbfd5abfd0d6ddf","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Nonuniqueness-for-the-periodic-hard-sphere-Boltzmann-equation-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L55"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere is a nonnegative density \\(F_0\\) on \\(\\T^3\\times\\R^3\\), with bounded\nvelocity support and\n\\[\n\\int_{\\T^3\\times\\R^3}\n F_0(1+|v|^2+|\\log F_0|)\\dd x\\dd v<\\infty,\n\\]\nfor which the hard-sphere Boltzmann equation has two distinct global\nadmissible solutions, in the sense of Definition~\\ref{def:admissible},\nwith initial datum \\(F_0\\).\nOn some common initial interval both solutions are strongly continuous\nin \\(L^1\\), and their collision gains and losses are integrable in\nspace-time-velocity."}
